[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3488005692","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-3488005692","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":3488005692,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7P5r48","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-04T21:03:37Z","updated_at":"2025-11-04T21:03:37Z","body":"Without looking at this in detail, this could be because of this:\n\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/physics/using_jolt_physics.html#single-body-joints","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3488005692/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3499386131","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-3499386131","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":3499386131,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7QlGUT","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-06T21:03:58Z","updated_at":"2025-11-06T21:03:58Z","body":"I've confirmed that the difference in behavior can be fixed by switching the setting mentioned above, so this is not a bug.\n\nNote that switching the setting causes the scene to behave like https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112365. The fix is the same: remove the rotational axis lock.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3499386131/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3503632634","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-3503632634","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":3503632634,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q1TD6","user":{"login":"GorgWorgington","id":9775975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk3NzU5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9775975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington","html_url":"https://github.com/GorgWorgington","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GorgWorgington/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T16:51:23Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T16:51:23Z","body":"It may be documented but it definitely feels like a bug when you stumble upon it. Is there a particular reason the default jolt behavior doesn't match the GodotPhysics behavior?\n\nI suppose #112365 was responsible for a lot of the confusion since I did try changing that setting at one point and got some extremely cursed behavior.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3503632634/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3504525621","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-3504525621","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":3504525621,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Q4tE1","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-07T19:35:14Z","updated_at":"2025-11-07T19:35:14Z","body":"> Is there a particular reason the default jolt behavior doesn't match the GodotPhysics behavior?\n\nYes, because the default behavior in Godot Physics makes absolutely no sense. If you think about limits, you visualize them as being attached to the static world and the object that's constrained moving within those limits. With Godot Physics it's the other way around: the limits are attached to the moving object and it is the static world that is limited in movement. This is still kind of understandable when you work with simple constraints like hinges and sliders, but when you start using a Generic6DOFJoint3D things become impossible to understand. This makes it very hard to properly configure the limits.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3504525621/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4937677183","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-4937677183","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":4937677183,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJk75fw","user":{"login":"AleMarcati","id":91221462,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMjIxNDYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91221462?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati","html_url":"https://github.com/AleMarcati","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-10T17:04:16Z","updated_at":"2026-07-10T17:04:16Z","body":"@jrouwe I just tested it and setting some other PhysicsBody to NodeA in the hinge does not fix the inverted limits. It's still inverted wether it has a Node set to NodeA or not. Did I misunderstand?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4937677183/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4945985651","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-4945985651","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":4945985651,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJs3Acw","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T12:42:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T12:42:49Z","body":"If you want to mimic the behavior of Godot Physics, you need to set the door's rigid body (in MRP: `RigidBody3D`) to be NodeA and the 'other body' to NodeB.\n\nIn Godot Physics, if one of the nodes is empty, it doesn't matter if you set NodeA or NodeB. It is always treated as NodeA. In the MRP above, this means you attach the world to NodeB instead of attaching NodeB to the world. Both work, but the change of perspective flips the limits.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4945985651/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4947218795","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-4947218795","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":4947218795,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJuCRaw","user":{"login":"AleMarcati","id":91221462,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMjIxNDYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91221462?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati","html_url":"https://github.com/AleMarcati","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T15:42:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T15:53:44Z","body":"Ok, that seems to work. Thank you for clearing that up.\nI think the tooltips should mention that if one of the bodies is a fixed body (like a static body), it should be set to node B and the movable body should be set to node A.\nAlso the gizmo should have some better indication of what is the upper and what is the lower limit. The respective lines could have different colors, like green for lower and red for upper, and maybe arrows indicating the direction the angles increase in the circle (a way to indicate that the hinge is \"right-handed\" if +Z is the \"thumb\"). Those things would make it much less confusing to set up the hinge.\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4947218795/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948428411","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-4948428411","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":4948428411,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJvMGew","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T19:14:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T19:14:51Z","body":"> I think the tooltips should mention that if one of the bodies is a fixed body (like a static body), it should be set to node B and the movable body should be set to node A.\n\nThis is how Godot Physics defines things, but I think it should be the opposite: You want to attach a dynamic body to the world, not the world to a dynamic body (don't want the tail wagging the dog).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948428411/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948889404","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112362#issuecomment-4948889404","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/112362","id":4948889404,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABJvoPPA","user":{"login":"AleMarcati","id":91221462,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkxMjIxNDYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/91221462?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati","html_url":"https://github.com/AleMarcati","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AleMarcati/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-11T21:52:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-11T21:52:34Z","body":"@jrouwe yes, I agree. But however it should work, the way it works should be made clear in the tooltips as to avoid this kind of confusion. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4948889404/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]